#!/usr/bin/env man

.TH simple_shell 1
.Dd 01/2026
.Dt simple_shell
.Os Linux
.Sh NAME
.Nm simple_shell
.Nd simple UNIX command line interpreter
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm simple_shell
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
program is a simple UNIX command line interpreter that reads commands
from standard input and executes them.

It works in both interactive and non-interactive modes.
The shell displays a prompt then takes the user input, searches for executable
files using the PATH environment variable and executes programs.

The shell supports basic command execution and a limited set of
built-in commands (exit and env).
.Sh FEATURES
.Bl -bullet
.It
Displays a prompt ("$ ") in interactive mode
.It
Executes commands with arguments
.It
Searches for executables in directories listed in PATH
.It
Supports built-in commands:
.Cm exit
and
.Cm env
.It
Handles absolute paths and relative paths
.It
Works in non-interactive mode using standard input
.El
.Sh BUILT-IN COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Cm exit
Exits the shell and terminates the program.
.It Cm env
Prints the current environment variables.
.El
.Sh USAGE
.Sh Interactive mode
To start the shell in interactive mode, run:
.Pp
.Dl ./simple_shell
.Pp
The shell will display a prompt and wait for user input.
.Sh Non-interactive mode
The shell can read commands from standard input:
.Pp
.Dl echo "/bin/ls" | ./simple_shell
.Pp
Or from a file:
.Pp
.Dl cat script | ./simple_shell
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Pp
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It ./simple_shell
Starts the shell in interactive mode.
.It ls -l
Lists files in the current directory.
.It /bin/pwd
Prints the current working directory.
.It env
Prints the environment variables.
.It exit
Exits the shell.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Pp
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It main.h
Header file containing function prototypes and includes.
.It simple_shell.c
Main loop of the shell, reads input and processes commands.
.It arr_strtok.c
Splits a string into an array of tokens.
.It strtok_arr_len.c
Calculates the number of tokens needed for allocation.
.It ev_exec_cmd.c
Evaluates commands and handles built-ins and execution logic.
.It fork_shell.c
Forks processes and executes commands.
.It find_path.c
Searches for executable paths using PATH.
.It print_env.c
Prints environment variables.
.It free_args.c
Frees a 2D array of strings.
.It exit_shell.c
Handles exiting the shell.
.El
.Sh RETURN VALUE
.Pp
The simple_shell program returns the exit status of the last command written in the shell.
.Pp
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It 0
Returned when no command is executed or when input is simply empty.
.It 2
Returned after a successful command execution.
.It 127
Returned when a command is not found in the system.
.El
.Pp
The shell terminates immediately when the built-in command
.Cm exit
is executed or when an end-of-file condition (Ctrl+D) is received.

.Sh ERRORS
If a command cannot be found or executed, the shell prints an error
message to standard error and continues execution.
.Sh BUGS
This shell does not support:
.Pp
.Bl -bullet
.It
Pipes
.It
Redirections
.It
Logical operators (&&, ||)
.It
Command separators (;)
.It
Signal handling (Ctrl+C)
.El
